   "Statement": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\">\r\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\r\n\t<head>\r\n\t\t<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" /><title>\r\n\t\t</title>\r\n\t\t<style type=\"text/css\">\r\n\t\t\t.cs778DBFE2{text-align:left;text-indent:0pt;margin:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto}\r\n\t\t\t.csAC9CF2{color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-family:Arial;font-size:21pt;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal;}\r\n\t\t\t.cs5E98E930{color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal;}\r\n\t\t\t.csA16174BA{color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;}\r\n\t\t</style>\r\n\t</head>\r\n\t<body>\r\n\t\t<p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><strong><span class=\"cs5E98E930\">Education: </span></strong></em><span class=\"csA16174BA\">JD, Seattle University; BA, University of Washington</span></strong></em></p><p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><strong><span class=\"cs5E98E930\">Occupation: </span></strong></em><span class=\"csA16174BA\">Judge Pro Tem and Maple Valley Prosecuting Attorney</span></strong></em></p><p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><strong><span class=\"cs5E98E930\">Statement: </span></strong></em><span class=\"csA16174BA\">Tricia Grove Johnson was born and raised in Southeast King County and has devoted her 30-year legal career to serving the community she calls home. Her extensive background&mdash;spanning Prosecution, Criminal Defense, Public Defense, and hundreds of hours &nbsp;as a Judge Pro Tem&mdash;gives her a rare, comprehensive understanding of the justice system and the people it impacts.</span></strong></em></p><p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><span class=\"csA16174BA\">Tricia has worked closely with individuals in crisis and with communities that have historically faced barriers within the legal system. She believes &nbsp;that true justice requires a balance of Accountability, Compassion, and Opportunities. Accountability ensures safer communities. Compassion recognizes the humanity and circumstances of every person. Opportunities create pathways for individuals to rebuild, grow, and contribute positively to their community.</span></strong></em></p><p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><span class=\"csA16174BA\">Her approach is rooted in the idea that a justice system must protect the public while also offering meaningful chances for change. She is committed to serving with integrity and &nbsp;ensuring that every person who enters the courtroom is treated with dignity and respect. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></strong></em></p><p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><span class=\"csA16174BA\">Endorsed by: &nbsp;Mayors of Maple Valley, Renton, Kent, Auburn, National Women&rsquo;s Political Caucus of Washington; and IAM 751, Amalgamated Transit Union Local 587, King County Democrats, and rated &ldquo;Exceptionally Well Qualified&rdquo; by five independent Bar Associations</span></strong></em></p></body>\r\n</html>\r\n",
